[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-32-15 for furnishing one new hydraulic excavator and one new 30
ton articulated dump truck for the City’s Landfill Division (Solid Waste Management) -- referred
to Finance Committee.
Appointment of John D. Hall as City Engineer.  Mr. Shanor moved to approve, seconded by
Mr. Brown.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present with the
exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote (Mayoral appointee).

Appointment of Paul Pomeroy,to the Contractor Licensing Board.  Mr. Brown moved to
approve, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing
body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not vote (Mayoral appointee).
Re-Appointment of Scott Cowley to the Cheyenne/Laramie County Economic Development
Joint Powers Board.  Mr. Shanor moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Motion carried.  Voting
“yes” -- all members of the governing body present with the exception of Mayor Kaysen who did not
vote (Mayoral appointee).
[CA]
Request to approve an additional dispensing room for City of Cheyenne Limited Retail
Liquor Licensee Fraternal Order of Eagles Aerie #128, located at 1600 Thomes Avenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming -- referred to Finance Commitee.
Announcement was made of the Appointments of Allison Anderson and Kiersti Willms, to
the Laramie County Community Juvenile Services Joint Powers Board, to be confirmed July 13,
2015.
Under other business, Frank Cole expressed his concerns regarding mowing of prairie grass
along a portion of the Greenway off Dell Range Blvd., suggesting mowing for the season not begin
until wild flowers had stopped blooming.  He submitted photos of the area (on file in office of City
Clerk) in conjunction with his comments.  Ms. Williams requested review of mowing operations in
several South Cheyenne areas, noting that not everything is being completely mowed.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 6:18  p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC

City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
June 29, 2015
